{"content":"💡 **SUGGESTION: version parsed from pubspec is unvalidated, and create-failure is swallowed without a trace**

1. `version=$(sed -n 's/^version: //p' pubspec.yaml)` — if the line is missing/malformed (merge accident, sed collision), `tag` becomes bare `v` and the script attempts `git tag -a v` / `gh release create v`. A one-line sanity check turns that into a clear failure:

```bash
case "$version" in
  [0-9]*.[0-9]*.[0-9]*) ;;
  *) echo "::error::unexpected pubspec version '$version'"; exit 1 ;;
esac
```

2. `gh release create ... || true` swallows *every* failure mode (auth, network, tag-not-yet-visible) with zero signal. At minimum emit `echo "::warning::gh release create failed — binaries attach_or_create fallback will mint a bare release"` before continuing, so the notes degradation (see comment on missing GH_TOKEN) is visible in the run summary.
","path":"outputs/pr_review_comments/comment7.md"}

{"content":"💡 **SUGGESTION: hygiene suite pins the script text but not the workflow wiring — the exact class of bug this PR ships with**

Two gaps in the new contract tests:

1. `expect(tagScript, contains('RELEASE_PAT'))` (this line) is satisfied by the **comment** on `scripts/tag_release.sh:5` — the actual token wiring lives in `ci.yml`'s `release-tag` checkout (`token: ${{ secrets.RELEASE_PAT }}`), which nothing asserts. Deleting that `token:` line keeps the suite green while killing the tag-scoped binaries/publish trigger — the failure mode the test exists to prevent.
2. No assertion pins `GH_TOKEN` on the `release` (bump) or `release-tag` steps at all — which is precisely why the missing-env bug (see inline comments on `auto_release.sh:145` / `tag_release.sh:27`) passes CI today.

Suggested additions to the same test:

```dart
final ci = read('.github/workflows/ci.yml');
// bump step must call gh with a token: RELEASE_PAT env (github.token PRs
// don't fire downstream machine events)
expect(RegExp(r'Bump version, changelog, open release PR[\s\S]*?GH_TOKEN:\s*\$\{\{ secrets\.RELEASE_PAT \}\}')
    .hasMatch(ci), isTrue,
    reason: 'release job must export GH_TOKEN=RELEASE_PAT — gh is unauthenticated on runners otherwise');
// release-tag checkout must ride RELEASE_PAT so the pushed tag fires tag-scoped jobs
expect(RegExp(r'release-tag:[\s\S]*?token:\s*\$\{\{ secrets\.RELEASE_PAT \}\}').hasMatch(ci), isTrue);
```

(This review found the runtime gap the current text-only assertions cannot see — worth encoding the workflow wiring, not just the scripts.)
